{"id": "000VJL", "title": "Yin Yang: Polar Arrows", "posted": "Heute, 01:07 Uhr", "author": "Vythic", "rules": "Play on SudokuPad!\n\nPlace a digit 1-9 in each cell. Digits do not repeat in rows or columns.\n\nShade some cells such that all shaded cells are orthogonally connected, all unshaded cells are orthogonally connected, and no 2x2 cluster of cells is entirely shaded or unshaded. Every orthogonal path that is fully contained within shaded cells must increase or decrease, with 1 and 9 reversing the direction. Every orthogonal path along unshaded cells must do the same.\n\nA digit on an arrow indicates the number of cells in the direction of the arrow that share its shading or lack thereof, not counting the arrow cell. If the digit is a 4 or higher, it counts cells in the opposite direction, not counting the arrow cell.\n\nCells on a thermometer are either all shaded or all unshaded. Digits along a thermometer increase from the bulb.", "solutionCode": "Row 2, left to right, with a comma between digits of different shading", "difficulty": 4, "solvedCount": 3, "tags": ["Sudoku", "Pfeile", "Yin und Yang", "Thermometer"], "links": [{"url": "https://sudokupad.app/6k5jqzldvf", "kind": "sudokupad"}], "firstSeen": "2026-10-17T17:00:00+00:00", "data": "", "link": "https://sudokupad.app/6k5jqzldvf", "linkKind": "sudokupad", "settings": {}, "summary": {"format": "scl", "decoded": true, "rows": 9, "cols": 9, "cages": 0, "hasSolution": true, "features": ["lines", "arrows", "underlays"]}}